# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# |<----  Using a Maximum Of 50 Characters  ----|
#
# Explain why this change is being made
# |<----  Try To Limit Each Line to a Maximum Of 72 Characters  ----|
#
# Provide links to any relevant tickets, PRs or other resources
# Example: Closes #123, Related to #456
#
# ---------- CONVENTIONAL COMMIT TYPES ----------
# feat:     A new feature
# fix:      A bug fix
# docs:     Documentation only changes
# style:    Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
#           (formatting, missing semicolons, etc)
# refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf:     A code change that improves performance
# test:     Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# chore:    Changes to build process, dependencies, or tooling
# ci:       Changes to CI/CD configuration
#
# ---------- SCOPE EXAMPLES ----------
# api:        API routes and endpoints
# repo:       Repository/database layer
# db:         Database schema or migrations
# store:      Zustand state management
# meal:       Meal logging feature
# supplement: Supplement tracking feature
# profile:    User profile feature
# analytics:  Analytics and reporting
# ui:         UI components and styling
# form:       Form components
# hook:       Custom React hooks
# types:      TypeScript types and interfaces
# util:       Utility functions and helpers
#
# ---------- ATOMIC COMMIT CHECKLIST ----------
# Before committing, ensure:
# ✓ One logical change per commit
# ✓ Each commit is independently testable
# ✓ No mixed concerns (e.g., feat + refactor)
# ✓ All tests pass locally (npm test)
# ✓ Linting passes locally (npm run lint)
# ✓ TypeScript passes (npx tsc --noEmit)
# ✓ Related files modified together
# ✓ Tests added/updated for code changes
#
# ---------- PRECOMMIT CHECKS ----------
# Husky + lint-staged automatically:
# → Runs ESLint with --fix on *.{js,jsx,ts,tsx}
# → Formats with Prettier on changed files
# → Runs tests on modified components
#
# All checks must pass before commit completes.
# If checks fail, fix the issues and stage again.
#
# ---------- EXAMPLES ----------
# Regular feature:
# feat(meal): add allergen conflict detection
#
# Bug fix:
# fix(meal): prevent duplicate food entries
#
# Database change:
# chore(db): add indexes to meal_logs table
#
# Component improvement:
# refactor(analytics): extract chart logic to hook
#
# With body and references:
# feat(api): implement daily summary endpoint
#
# Aggregates daily nutritional and supplement data,
# returns health score and nutrient totals for dashboard.
#
# Closes #123
#
# --------------------------------------------------
